=====================================================================
Statement of changes (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b))
=====================================================================

The following files were added or modified relative to upstream OOOSplat.
No upstream functionality was removed.

ADDED (this project's contribution — see docs/DESIGN.md):

  src-tauri/src/reconstruction/colmap.rs
      COLMAP sparse-reconstruction reader (cameras.bin / images.bin /
      points3D.bin) and camera projection mathematics, with unit tests
      that verify the binary layout by round-trip against synthetic files.

  src-tauri/src/reconstruction/inspect.rs
      Project audit: frame counts, camera registration ratio, camera
      intrinsics, sparse point statistics, and a readiness check that
      decides whether a reconstruction can be used for auto-annotation.

  src-tauri/src/reconstruction/autolabel.rs
      3D bounding-box fitting from the sparse point cloud (with the up
      axis inferred from the camera trajectory), projection of that box
      into every registered frame, per-frame quality checks, YOLO label
      export, CSV/JSON reports and a dependency-free HTML review sheet.

  docs/DESIGN.md, docs/COMPLIANCE.md
      Design rationale and licensing/originality statement.

MODIFIED (product identity and CLI surface only; no upstream logic changed):

  package.json                 name: "ooo-splat"  -> "macausplat"
  src-tauri/tauri.conf.json    productName/title: "OOOSplat" -> "MacauSplat"
                               (identifier "studio.ooo.splat" intentionally
                                left unchanged so existing settings and the
                                project index keep working)
  src-tauri/src/lib.rs         window failure message text
  src-tauri/src/bin/splatstudio.rs
                               CLI description text; added three subcommands:
                               `inspect`, `fit-box`, `annotate`
  src-tauri/src/reconstruction/mod.rs
                               registered the three new modules
  README.md                    added a project banner
  TRADEMARK_POLICY.md          retained verbatim (upstream document)

UNCHANGED: the reconstruction pipeline itself (FFmpeg frame extraction,
COLMAP feature extraction/mapping, Brush training, PLY publishing, Gaussian
preview, editing, animation export, telemetry).

